{"thread":{"threadID":4944,"boardID":125,"topic":"FPS","time":1510323170,"userID":2165,"username":"Makaveli1967","lastPostTime":1510411848,"lastPoster":"Makaveli1967","replies":21,"views":485,"attachments":0,"isSticky":0,"isClosed":1,"cumulativeLikes":0},"tags":[],"posts":[{"postID":73762,"threadID":4944,"userID":2165,"username":"Makaveli1967","subject":"FPS","time":1510323170,"lastEditTime":0,"editCount":0,"editReason":null,"attachments":[],"cumulativeLikes":0,"editorID":null,"editor":"","likes":[],"bodyHtml":"<p>Seit dem ich auf Windows 10 gewechselt habe, habe ich FPS Drops.<br>Und wenn es mal konstant ist, habe ich max 50 wobei ich normalerweise 70 habe.<br>Kann mir jemand helfen?</p>","polls":[]},{"postID":73763,"threadID":4944,"userID":2229,"username":"WHAT","subject":"","time":1510324105,"lastEditTime":0,"editCount":0,"editReason":null,"attachments":[],"cumulativeLikes":2,"editorID":null,"editor":"","likes":[{"userID":1825,"username":"Nachtfrische","time":1510329018,"value":1},{"userID":1173,"username":"Nightlight","time":1510332213,"value":1}],"bodyHtml":"<p>Try to turn off &quot;Xbox DVR&quot; that usually helps. Here is some info and help</p>\n<p><br></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://support.steampowered.com/kb_article.php?ref=6239-DZCB-8600\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\"></a></p>\n<p><br></p>\n<p><span class=\"metacode-inline\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sU6DFUgBE4g</span></p>\n<p><br></p>\n<p>Hope it works!</p>\n<p><br></p>\n<p><span class=\"missing-media\">[Bild]</span></p>","polls":[]},{"postID":73764,"threadID":4944,"userID":2165,"username":"Makaveli1967","subject":"","time":1510324304,"lastEditTime":0,"editCount":0,"editReason":null,"attachments":[],"cumulativeLikes":0,"editorID":null,"editor":"","likes":[],"bodyHtml":"<blockquote class=\"archive-quote\"><cite>Zitat von <strong>WHAT</strong></cite><p>Try to turn off &quot;Xbox DVR&quot; that usually helps. Here is some info and help</p>\n<p><br></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://support.steampowered.com/kb_article.php?ref=6239-DZCB-8600\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\"></a></p>\n<p><br></p>\n<p><span class=\"metacode-inline\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sU6DFUgBE4g</span></p>\n<p><br></p>\n<p>Hope it works!</p>\n<p><br></p>\n<p><span class=\"missing-media\">[Bild]</span><br></p></blockquote><p>I&#x27;ll try it out.<br>Thanks!</p>","polls":[]},{"postID":73766,"threadID":4944,"userID":2165,"username":"Makaveli1967","subject":"","time":1510325301,"lastEditTime":0,"editCount":0,"editReason":null,"attachments":[],"cumulativeLikes":0,"editorID":null,"editor":"","likes":[],"bodyHtml":"<p>Didn&#x27;t really fix my problem</p>","polls":[]},{"postID":73767,"threadID":4944,"userID":2369,"username":"Luckiris","subject":"","time":1510326111,"lastEditTime":0,"editCount":0,"editReason":null,"attachments":[],"cumulativeLikes":0,"editorID":null,"editor":"","likes":[],"bodyHtml":"<p>By switching to Windows 10, did you have any other problem ?</p>","polls":[]},{"postID":73768,"threadID":4944,"userID":2165,"username":"Makaveli1967","subject":"","time":1510327158,"lastEditTime":0,"editCount":0,"editReason":null,"attachments":[],"cumulativeLikes":0,"editorID":null,"editor":"","likes":[],"bodyHtml":"<blockquote class=\"archive-quote\"><cite>Zitat von <strong>Luckiris</strong></cite><p>By switching to Windows 10, did you have any other problem ?<br></p></blockquote><p>Nope</p>","polls":[]},{"postID":73770,"threadID":4944,"userID":1825,"username":"Nachtfrische","subject":"","time":1510329158,"lastEditTime":0,"editCount":0,"editReason":null,"attachments":[],"cumulativeLikes":0,"editorID":null,"editor":"","likes":[],"bodyHtml":"<p>Wenn dir Xbox DVR nichts gebracht hat, probier mal den Windows 10 Game Mode auszuschalten.<br>Falls das nichts bringt, deinstallier deine Grafikkartentreiber über DDU (Display Driver Uninstaller) im abgesicherteren Modus und installier sie dann nach einem Reboot neu.</p>","polls":[]},{"postID":73771,"threadID":4944,"userID":2053,"username":"coldenes","subject":"","time":1510329683,"lastEditTime":0,"editCount":0,"editReason":null,"attachments":[],"cumulativeLikes":0,"editorID":null,"editor":"","likes":[],"bodyHtml":"<p><a href=\"https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1081885587\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\"></a> hat mir sehr geholfen.</p>","polls":[]},{"postID":73773,"threadID":4944,"userID":2165,"username":"Makaveli1967","subject":"","time":1510335391,"lastEditTime":0,"editCount":0,"editReason":null,"attachments":[],"cumulativeLikes":0,"editorID":null,"editor":"","likes":[],"bodyHtml":"<blockquote class=\"archive-quote\"><cite>Zitat von <strong>Nachtfrische</strong></cite><p>probier mal den Windows 10 Game Mode auszuschalten<br></p></blockquote><p>Und wie soll dass gehen?<br>In den Einstellungen gibt es keine Optionen dafür.<br><a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/iKtF7\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\"></a></p>","polls":[]},{"postID":73776,"threadID":4944,"userID":1749,"username":"CyberTroniX","subject":"","time":1510344327,"lastEditTime":0,"editCount":0,"editReason":"","attachments":[],"cumulativeLikes":0,"editorID":null,"editor":"","likes":[],"bodyHtml":"<blockquote class=\"archive-quote\"><cite>Zitat von <strong>Makaveli1967</strong></cite><p>Und wie soll dass gehen?In den Einstellungen gibt es keine Optionen dafür.<br><a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/iKtF7\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\"></a><br></p></blockquote><p><a href=\"https://gyazo.com/b5c149ac41914710fe903d16baadf61f\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\"> Game Mode.gif </a></p>","polls":[]},{"postID":73777,"threadID":4944,"userID":2165,"username":"Makaveli1967","subject":"","time":1510345776,"lastEditTime":0,"editCount":0,"editReason":null,"attachments":[],"cumulativeLikes":0,"editorID":null,"editor":"","likes":[],"bodyHtml":"<blockquote class=\"archive-quote\"><cite>Zitat von <strong>CyberTroniX</strong></cite><p><a href=\"https://gyazo.com/b5c149ac41914710fe903d16baadf61f\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\"> Game Mode.gif </a><br></p></blockquote><p>Ist bei mir nicht.</p>","polls":[]},{"postID":73778,"threadID":4944,"userID":1749,"username":"CyberTroniX","subject":"","time":1510347319,"lastEditTime":0,"editCount":0,"editReason":null,"attachments":[],"cumulativeLikes":1,"editorID":null,"editor":"","likes":[{"userID":1825,"username":"Nachtfrische","time":1510347650,"value":1}],"bodyHtml":"<blockquote class=\"archive-quote\"><cite>Zitat von <strong>Makaveli1967</strong></cite><p>Ist bei mir nicht.<br></p></blockquote><p><a href=\"https://www.windowscentral.com/how-enable-disable-game-mode-windows-10-creators-update\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">How to enable/disable Game Mode [Windows 10]</a></p>","polls":[]},{"postID":73780,"threadID":4944,"userID":1825,"username":"Nachtfrische","subject":"","time":1510347644,"lastEditTime":0,"editCount":0,"editReason":null,"attachments":[],"cumulativeLikes":0,"editorID":null,"editor":"","likes":[],"bodyHtml":"<blockquote class=\"archive-quote\"><cite>Zitat von <strong>Makaveli1967</strong></cite><p>Ist bei mir nicht.<br></p></blockquote><p>Sicher, dass du auf der neusten Windows Version bist? Die neue Version hat tatsächlich ein paar Performanceoptimierungen bezüglich Gaming. Öffne mal die Einstellungen, dann geh auf System -&gt; Info und schau dir den &quot;Betriebssystembuild&quot; an. Der sollte 16299 sein. Falls er es nicht ist, würde ich dir empfehlen, dein Windows manuell upzudaten.</p>\n<p><br></p>\n<p>Du kannst <a href=\"https://www.microsoft.com/de-de/software-download//windows10\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">hier drauf</a> gehen und dann auf &quot;Jetzt aktualisieren&quot; klicken und kriegst dann ein Tool von Microsoft, welches das Update herunterlädt.</p>","polls":[]},{"postID":73781,"threadID":4944,"userID":2165,"username":"Makaveli1967","subject":"","time":1510347761,"lastEditTime":0,"editCount":0,"editReason":null,"attachments":[],"cumulativeLikes":0,"editorID":null,"editor":"","likes":[],"bodyHtml":"<p>Jap<br><a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/dd3vr\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\"></a><br></p>\n<blockquote class=\"archive-quote\"><cite>Zitat von <strong>Nachtfrische</strong></cite><p>Sicher, dass du auf der neusten Windows Version bist? Die neue Version hat tatsächlich ein paar Performanceoptimierungen bezüglich Gaming. Öffne mal die Einstellungen, dann geh auf System -&gt; Info und schau dir den &quot;Betriebssystembuild&quot; an. Der sollte 16299 sein. Falls er es nicht ist, würde ich dir empfehlen, dein Windows manuell upzudaten.<br>Du kannst <a href=\"https://www.microsoft.com/de-de/software-download//windows10\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">hier drauf</a> gehen und dann auf &quot;Jetzt aktualisieren&quot; klicken und kriegst dann ein Tool von Microsoft, welches das Update herunterlädt.<br></p></blockquote>","polls":[]},{"postID":73782,"threadID":4944,"userID":2165,"username":"Makaveli1967","subject":"","time":1510349877,"lastEditTime":0,"editCount":0,"editReason":null,"attachments":[],"cumulativeLikes":0,"editorID":null,"editor":"","likes":[],"bodyHtml":"<p>Jemand ne Hilfe für mich?<br>Sonst muss ich diesen Dreck entfernen und Win 7 benutzen.</p>","polls":[]},{"postID":73790,"threadID":4944,"userID":1749,"username":"CyberTroniX","subject":"","time":1510391532,"lastEditTime":0,"editCount":0,"editReason":null,"attachments":[],"cumulativeLikes":0,"editorID":null,"editor":"","likes":[],"bodyHtml":"<p>Kannst du mal einen Screenshot von deinem Einstellungs-Menü senden?<br>Wäre evtl. hilfreich, danke. <span class=\"archive-emoji\">😄</span></p>","polls":[]},{"postID":73791,"threadID":4944,"userID":2165,"username":"Makaveli1967","subject":"","time":1510394757,"lastEditTime":1510398204,"editCount":2,"editReason":"","attachments":[],"cumulativeLikes":0,"editorID":2165,"editor":"Makaveli1967","likes":[],"bodyHtml":"<blockquote class=\"archive-quote\"><cite>Zitat von <strong>Makaveli1967</strong></cite><p><a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/iKtF7\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\"></a><br></p><span class=\"quote-missing\">Zitierter Inhalt ist im Dump nicht eingebettet.</span></blockquote><p><br></p>\n<blockquote class=\"archive-quote\"><cite>Zitat von <strong>CyberTroniX</strong></cite><p>Kannst du mal einen Screenshot von deinem Einstellungs-Menü senden?<br>Wäre evtl. hilfreich, danke. <span class=\"archive-emoji\">😄</span> <br></p></blockquote><p>Dass habe ich bereits</p>\n<p><br></p>\n<p>Hier noch ein Screen wenn du es willst.<br><span class=\"missing-media\">[Bild]</span></p>","polls":[]},{"postID":73793,"threadID":4944,"userID":2165,"username":"Makaveli1967","subject":"","time":1510403355,"lastEditTime":0,"editCount":0,"editReason":"","attachments":[],"cumulativeLikes":0,"editorID":null,"editor":"","likes":[],"bodyHtml":"<p><a href=\"https://dream-community.de/index.php?user/1825-nachtfrische/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">@Nachtfrische</a> <a href=\"https://dream-community.de/index.php?user/1749-cybertronix/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">@CyberTroniX</a><br>Dass war die Ursache wieso es nicht ging.<br><a href=\"https://www.tenforums.com/tutorials/75936-turn-off-game-mode-windows-10-a.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\"></a><br></p>\n<blockquote class=\"archive-quote\"><cite>Zitat von <strong>Tenforums</strong></cite><p>In <a href=\"https://www.tenforums.com/windows-10-news/75916-announcing-windows-10-insider-preview-build-15019-pc.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\"><strong>Windows 10 build 15019</strong></a>, Game Mode is enabled system wide by default, however, the ON/OFF toggle in Settings will incorrectly show it as being OFF until the user manually toggles the Setting to ON which will cause it to update and accurately display the status of Game Mode system wide.</p>\n<p><br></p>\n<p><span class=\"missing-media\">[Bild]</span> This setting is no longer available starting in <strong>Windows 10 Fall Creators Update</strong> <a href=\"https://www.tenforums.com/tutorials/32961-find-windows-10-version-number.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\"><strong>version 1709</strong></a>.<br></p></blockquote><p>Habe es damit nun deaktiviert und nun sieht es in den Einstellungen so aus.<br><a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/pL3tB\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\"></a></p>\n<p><br></p>\n<p>Mal schauen ob es jetzt besser funktioniert.</p>","polls":[]},{"postID":73798,"threadID":4944,"userID":2165,"username":"Makaveli1967","subject":"","time":1510408251,"lastEditTime":0,"editCount":0,"editReason":null,"attachments":[],"cumulativeLikes":0,"editorID":null,"editor":"","likes":[],"bodyHtml":"<p>Problem immer noch vorhanden, bitte um Hilfe.</p>","polls":[]},{"postID":73799,"threadID":4944,"userID":1749,"username":"CyberTroniX","subject":"","time":1510408292,"lastEditTime":0,"editCount":0,"editReason":null,"attachments":[],"cumulativeLikes":0,"editorID":null,"editor":"","likes":[],"bodyHtml":"<blockquote class=\"archive-quote\"><cite>Zitat von <strong>Makaveli1967</strong></cite><p><a href=\"https://dream-community.de/index.php?user/1825-nachtfrische/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">@Nachtfrische</a> <a href=\"https://dream-community.de/index.php?user/1749-cybertronix/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">@CyberTroniX</a><br>Dass war die Ursache wieso es nicht ging.<br><a href=\"https://www.tenforums.com/tutorials/75936-turn-off-game-mode-windows-10-a.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\"></a><br></p>\n<p>Habe es damit nun deaktiviert und nun sieht es in den Einstellungen so aus.<a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/pL3tB\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\"></a></p>\n<p><br></p>\n<p>Mal schauen ob es jetzt besser funktioniert.<br></p></blockquote><p>Das <a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/Windows10/comments/770jw0/game_mode_1709/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">hier</a> sollte helfen. Ich rate dir den Post genaustens durchzulesen um ja keine Fehler zu machen. Ein Backup, soweit möglich, ist ebenfalls sinnvoll.</p>","polls":[]},{"postID":73801,"threadID":4944,"userID":2165,"username":"Makaveli1967","subject":"","time":1510410604,"lastEditTime":0,"editCount":0,"editReason":null,"attachments":[],"cumulativeLikes":0,"editorID":null,"editor":"","likes":[],"bodyHtml":"<blockquote class=\"archive-quote\"><cite>Zitat von <strong>CyberTroniX</strong></cite><p>Das <a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/Windows10/comments/770jw0/game_mode_1709/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">hier</a> sollte helfen. Ich rate dir den Post genaustens durchzulesen um ja keine Fehler zu machen. Ein Backup, soweit möglich, ist ebenfalls sinnvoll.<br></p></blockquote><p>Game DVR ist schon bei mir deaktiviert gewesen.<br>Habe trotzdem diese Schritte ausführlich ausgeführt und ich habe immer noch die selben Ergebnisse.<br>Windows 10 ist ja mal echt scheiße.<br>Da denke ich mir &quot;ach komm, Windows 10 kann ja gar nicht so scheiße sein wie ich es mir denke&quot; aber dass tut sich nun wahr stellen.</p>","polls":[]},{"postID":73803,"threadID":4944,"userID":2165,"username":"Makaveli1967","subject":"","time":1510411848,"lastEditTime":0,"editCount":0,"editReason":null,"attachments":[],"cumulativeLikes":0,"editorID":null,"editor":"","likes":[],"bodyHtml":"<p>Sorry für Doppelpost aber ich deinstalliere jetzt den Kack.<br>Closed bitte den Thread</p>","polls":[]}]}